From a8d03cd37fc9275ecff16f746cddb5c6a77a7778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:05:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] Optional S3 (Sia-S3) backend for the witness gateway's
 immutable cache

network/s3-witness-cache.mjs implements the gateway's existing {get, put}
contract (witnessKey) on S3: chain-namespaced, block-hash and request pinned
keys; an entry is used only if its format, chain id, block hash and full
request match; create-only writes (If-None-Match: *) with compare-exact on
412 and no overwrite; writes OFF unless archive: true (an archived proof
names the accounts and slots read); bounded, timed-out, non-blocking writes
and reads; close() reaps every request. Signing is curl's maintained SigV4
(--aws-sigv4) with the access key on curl's stdin, never argv or env.

It is evidence availability only: the gateway consults it after every live
upstream failed and only for block-hash-pinned requests, and Helios
re-verifies every witness against its signed head.

Tests: AWS signing-suite vectors (aws-c-auth 84a26ea1), a real MinIO server,
a fault-injecting fake S3, and real patched Helios (Base EVM) replaying A's
recorded real Base calls from S3, refusing a forged entry and a missing one.

(cherry picked from commit 73c11ec936f16b4a8e02ced829fa31ca7c32c0b4)
(cherry picked from commit 96b877b7c89d2b9ac54df9099c44f97ff841e378)
